## Instant Insanity (instant-insanity): generated by spec_backend.py (WorldSpec, path B: Lean description, Python rules) from the instructor statements.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##  1. There are four cubes. Each face of a cube is red, green, blue, white or yellow.
##  2. Each cube is given by its three pairs of opposite faces: cube 1: red and green, blue and white, red and yellow; cube 2: green and blue, yellow and red, white and white; cube 3: yellow and white, green and red, blue and blue; cube 4: blue and red, white and yellow, green and green.
##  3. You stack the four cubes in a column, each turned any way you like.
##  4. The column has four sides: front, back, left and right.
##  5. The goal is that each of the four sides of the column shows four different colours.
##
## Assumption ledger:
##   A-II1: "turned any way you like": each cube has one orientation object per distinct assignment of colours to the four sides (front, back, left, right); the top and bottom faces do not matter. Cube 1 has 24, cubes 2 to 4 have 16 (each has a pair of equal colours).
##   A-II2: "stack in a column": cubes are placed one at a time in the order 1, 2, 3, 4, each on the one before; cube 1 goes on the ground, which counts as placed from the start.
##   A-II3: "four different colours" on a side: two placed cubes showing the same colour on the same side is a losing state, so a partial column that cannot be completed is cut off at once.

## Propose initialize-instant-insanity when its conditions below hold.
sp {instant-insanity*propose*initialize-instant-insanity
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-instant-insanity ^task-operator false)
}

sp {instant-insanity*apply*initialize-instant-insanity
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-instant-insanity ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
